NUM-51: evaluate whole-number powers of negative numbers in math expressions

mathexpr_eval() returned 0 for x^y whenever x <= 0. That guard is needed for
a fractional power of a negative number, which has no real value (pow()
returns NaN), but it also turned (-3)^2 into 0 and (-2)^3 into 0. Call pow()
for a negative base when the exponent is a whole number; keep 0 for a
fractional exponent and for a zero base, as before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-51_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
index c39dff7..6452efb 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
@@ -709,8 +709,9 @@ double mathexpr_eval(MathExpr *expr, double (*getVariableValue) (int))
                 stackindex--;
                 if (stackindex < 0) break;
                 r2 = ExprStack[stackindex];
-		if (r2 <= 0.0) r2 = 0.0;
-		else r2 = pow(r2, r1);
+		// --- a negative base has a real power only for a whole exponent
+		if (r2 > 0.0 || (r2 < 0.0 && r1 == floor(r1))) r2 = pow(r2, r1);
+		else r2 = 0.0;
 		ExprStack[stackindex] = r2;
 		break;
         }
